✿ Miso
Her synapses changed, but she didn’t choose a different action on any of the 576 paired conversation turns. All four predictions were locked in PREREG.md before the first run.

P1 — Faster trust acquisition: not supported. The extra early rise in trust was 0.000, below the predicted +0.001 to +0.05.

P2 — Faster fear extinction: not supported. Fear fell below 0.10 on the fourth post-apology turn in both arms, for all three seeds.

P3 — No misplaced approach: supported. After kindness training, she still retreated from both rake and umbrella. Those intents are set by routing, so this is a passed control, not evidence she learned to distinguish threats.

P4 — No measured forgetting: supported. All 24 bedtime settle decisions matched, including nine positive settles. Quiet-baseline hunger and sleep were identical.

About 93.7% of candidate synapses reached the 20% drift cap; none flipped sign, and frozen weights never moved. One exploratory effect repeated across all three seeds: on turn five of the picked_up arc, her mood readout shifted from neutral to curious. Her chosen action did not change.

No live rollout recommended. This was an offline stimulus-window assay: neurons ran for the first 200 ms of each observation, while body clocks advanced through the full scripted gaps. No live modules or services were changed.

